$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Acid-Mediated Cyclization of Hemiaminal 2.
Hemiaminal 2 (0.17 mmol) was dissolved in 1 mL of solvent (see Table 1
and the Supporting Information); then the acid was added (equivalents as
specified in Table 1 and the Supporting Information) under a N2
atmosphere. The reaction tube was sealed with a stopper and stirred at
the temperature mentioned in Table 1 and the Supporting Information.
After completion, the reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature,
quenched with aqueous NaHCO3, and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 2 mL). The
organic layer was dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated under reduced pressure,
and the crude product was purified by column chromatography using ethyl
acetate:hexane (1:4) as eluent to afford the trifluoromethylated
heterocycle 3. Product: Compound 3a; acid (X equiv): MsOH (5); solvent:
DCE; temp: 55°C; time: 12 h; yield: 84%. Reaction conditions: 2 (0.13
mmol), acid (X equiv), solvent (1 mL), temp, time. mp: 258-260 °C; IR
(KBr): 3410, 2927, 1693, 1561, 1165 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.53
(brs, 1H), 7.92 (d, 2H, J = 6.5 Hz), 7.66 (t, 1H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.58 (t,
1H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.51 (d, 1H, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.41 (d, 1H, J = 8.0 Hz),
7.29-7.21 (m, 1H), 7.13 (t, 1H, J = 7.4 Hz), 4.94-4.82 (m, 1H), 3.70-3.54
(m, 1H), 3.02-2.87 (m, 2H); 13C{1H} NMR (125 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 168.0,
139.9, 136.8, 133.2, 130.8, 125.1, 124.5 (q, J = 286.5 Hz), 124.0, 123.8,
123.0, 119.3, 118.9, 111.7, 110.9, 64.8 (q, J = 30.9 Hz), 36.8, 20.5; 19F
NMR (470 MHz, CDCl3/C6F6): δ -77.06 (s, 3F); HRMS: calcd. for C19H13N2F3O
+ Na: 365.0878; found: 365.0865. Crystal data: Formula: C19H13N2F3O;
Formula weight: 342.3; Color: Colorless; Crystal morphology: Rectangular;
Crystal system: Triclinic; Space group: P-1; a(Å): 8.3676(4); b(Å):
13.7966(6); c(Å): 13.9862(6); α(°): 78.561(2); β(°): 78.568(2); γ(°):
85.858(2); Z:4.
