$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction conditions: A Schlenk tube charged with the Togni reagent (II)
(0.4 mmol, 126 mg, 2.0 equiv), CuTc (0.02 mmol, 4 mg, 0.1 equiv) and 1
(0.2 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was evacuated and backfilled with argon (this
sequence was repeated three times). MeCN (1.5 mL) was added into the
tube. The reaction tube was placed in a pre-heated 80 °C oil bath until
compound 1 was consumed completely. The mixture was allowed to cool to
room temperature. The mixture was purified by silica gel flash
chromatography (eluent: petroleum ether). The product 2 in moderate
yield. Compound 2b: 63 mg, 83%, a white solid. m.p. 147-149 °C; IR
(CH2Cl2): ν 3284, 2924, 1598, 1461, 1312, 1287, 1157, 1108, 1051, 814
cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 2.37 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 2.44 (s,
3H), 2.83 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 4.15 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H), 4.62 (t, J = 6.0
Hz, 1H), 6.99 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.07-7.10 (m, 2H), 7.14-7.18 (m, 1H),
7.30 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.74 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3, TMS): δ 20.3 (q, J = 1.5 Hz), 21.5, 27.6, 44.5, 123.8 (q, J =
269.1 Hz), 124.2 (q, J = 6.6 Hz), 127.2, 128.0, 128.3, 129.09 (q, J =
30.7 Hz), 129.15, 129.5, 129.8, 132.5, 136.3, 136.5, 143.7; 19F NMR (376
MHz, CDCl3): δ -68.8; MS (ESI) m/z: 399.1 (M+NH4 +, 100); HRMS (ESI)
Calcd. for C19H22F3N2O2S+ requires: 399.1349, Found: 399.1357.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk tube was used, sealed tube used
