$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical synthetic procedure (with 3a as an
example): Togni reagent (474 mg, 1.5 mmol) and CuI (19 mg, 0.1 mmol) was
added into a flame-dried vial with a magnetic stir bar, and then sealed
with a septum. After the vial was evacuated and backfilled with N2 for
three times, 2a (238 mg, 1.0 mmol) in DMF (2.0 mL) was then added via
syringe. The reaction mixture was heated to 80°C and stirred for 26 h
until the disappearance of substrate 2a as indicated by TLC. The
resulting mixture was concentrated and the residue was taken up in DCM.
The organic layer was washed with brine, dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated. Purification of the crude product by flash column
chromatography (silica gel, petroleum ether: ethyl acetate = 100:1).
Product 3a (238 mg, 78%) as yellowish liquid. (TF-Hymecromone) White
solid. M.p. 190-191°C; 1H-NMR (500 MHz, DMSO) δ 11.0 (s, 1H), 7.85 (d, J
= 9.0 Hz, 1H), 6.85 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H), 6.69 (s, 1H), 2.56 (s, 3H);
13C-NMR (DMSO, 125 MHz) δ 163.9, 157.0, 156.3, 155.2, 129.2, 125.0 (q, J
= 272.6 Hz), 114.4, 111.4, 109.7 (q, J = 29.2 Hz), 102.3, 15.9 (q, J =
3.7 Hz); 19F-NMR (470.2 MHz, DMSO) δ -52.2 (s, 3F); HRMS (ESI) m/z
calculated for C11H8F3O3 [M+H]+ : 245.0426, found 245.0426.
