$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The General Procedure for the Trifluoromethylation Reaction In an
oven-dried Schlenk tube, to the solution of free anilines (0.2 mmol) and
Togni reagent 3 (1.3-1.6 equiv) in DMF (1.0 mL), was added Ir(ppy)3 (1.5
mol%). Then, the tube was degassed and filled with nitrogen for three
times. The resulting reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature by
irradiation with blue LEDs (7 W, λmax= 455 nm) for 15-36 hours. When the
reaction was finished, saturated NaHCO3 solution (5 mL) was added into
the reaction mixture, and extracted with ethyl acetate for four times.
The combined organic layers was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by silica gel
chromatography or preparative TLC on GF 254. The desired
trifluoromethylated anilines. 4-chloro-2-(trifluoromethyl)aniline 2: 0.2
mmol; 1.6 equiv Togni reagent was used; 60% yield, brown oil; 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) = 7.39 (d, J = 2.0 Hz), 7.24 (dd, J = 8.8, 2.0 Hz, 1
H), 6.68 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.03 (s, 2 H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
(ppm) = 143.0 (d, J = 2.1 Hz), 132.8, 126.4 (q, J = 5.4 Hz), 124.1 (q, J
= 270.9 Hz), 122.4, 118.5, 114.8 (q, J = 30.8 Hz); 19F NMR (376 MHz,
CDCl3): δ (ppm) = -63.2; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C7H4ClF3N [M-H]-:
193.9990; found: 193.9990.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, regioselective, optimized on CF3 reactant, catalyst,
additives, and solvent, blue LEDs used (7W, 455nm), optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Visible-Light-Promoted Radical C-H Trifluoromethylation of Free Anilines
