$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The General Procedure for the
Trifluoromethylation Reaction In an oven-dried Schlenk tube, to the
solution of free anilines (0.2 mmol) and Togni reagent 3 (1.3-1.6 equiv)
in DMF (1.0 mL), was added Ir(ppy)3 (1.5 mol%). Then, the tube was
degassed and filled with nitrogen for three times. The resulting reaction
mixture was stirred at room temperature by irradiation with blue LEDs (7
W, λmax= 455 nm) for 15-36 hours. When the reaction was finished,
saturated NaHCO3 solution (5 mL) was added into the reaction mixture, and
extracted with ethyl acetate for four times. The combined organic layers
was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue
was purified by silica gel chromatography or preparative TLC on GF 254.
The desired trifluoromethylated anilines.
(4-amino-3-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)(piperidin-1-yl)metha none 21: 0.2
mmol; 1.6 equiv Togni reagent was used; 81% yield, white solid; m.p.
105-107 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) = 7.52 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1 H),
7.33 (dd, J = 8.4, 1.6 Hz, 1 H), 6.76 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1 H), 4.57 (s, 2
H), 3.54 (s, 4 H), 1.74-1.51 (m, 6 H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm)
= 169.6, 145.8 (d, J = 1.9 Hz), 132.1, 126.4 (q, J = 4.6 Hz), 124.6,
124.5 (q, J = 270.6 Hz), 116.8, 112.9 (q, J = 30.4 Hz), 26.1, 24.5; 19F
NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) = -63.0; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C13H14F3N2O [M-H]-: 271.1064; found:271.1068.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, regioselective, blue LEDs used (7W, 455nm)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Visible-Light-Promoted Radical C-H Trifluoromethylation of Free Anilines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Xie, Jin; Yuan, Xiangai; Abdukader, Ablimit; Zhu, Chengjian; Ma, Jing
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(6), 1768-1771

