$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction conditions: A Schlenk tube charged
with the Togni reagent (II) (0.4 mmol, 126 mg, 2.0 equiv), CuTc (0.02
mmol, 4 mg, 0.1 equiv) and 1 (0.2 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was evacuated and
backfilled with argon (this sequence was repeated three times). MeCN (1.5
mL) was added into the tube. The reaction tube was placed in a pre-heated
80 °C oil bath until compound 1 was consumed completely. The mixture was
allowed to cool to room temperature. The mixture was purified by silica
gel flash chromatography (eluent: petroleum ether). The product 2 in
moderate yield. Compound 2i: 35 mg, 76%, a white solid. m.p. 97-99 °C; IR
(CH2Cl2): ν 2947, 1607, 1501, 1432, 1290, 1150, 1100, 1040, 899, 808
cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 2.43 (td, J 1 = 8.0 Hz, J 2 = 1.2
Hz, 2H), 2.88 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 6.72-6.74 (m, 2H), 6.90
(d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.08 (d, J = 9.2 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3,
TMS): δ 20.6 (q, J = 1.5 Hz), 27.7, 55.3, 111.5, 113.9, 124.30 (q, J =
268.3 Hz), 124.31, 124.7 (q, J = 31.3 Hz), 128.5 (q, J = 6.5 Hz), 129.2,
137.4, 160.3; 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ -68.4; HRMS (EI) m/z calculated
for C12H11OF3 [M+] 228.0762, found 228.0763.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk tube was used, regioisomeric ratio=2:1, 62% yield, sealed tube
used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
