$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.3 Typical Procedure for Pd(OAc)2-Catalyzed
C-H Trifluoromethylation. In a 20 mL sealed tube, N-aryl benzamide 1a
(33.7 mg, 0.10 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 5-(trifluoromethyl)dibenzothiophenium
trifluoromethanesulfonate 2a (60.3 mg, 0.15 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Pd(OAc)2
(2.3 mg, 0.01 mmol, 10 mol %), Cu(OAc)2 (36.4 mg, 0.20 mmol, 2.0 equiv),
N-methylformamide L4 (87.6 uL, 1.5 mmol, 15 equiv), and trifluoroacetic
acid (74.3 uL, 1.0 mmol, 10 equiv) were dissolved in 1,2-dichloroethane
(3 mL) under N2 atmosphere. The reaction mixture was then tightly capped
and stirred for 10 minutes at room temperature for proper mixing of the
reactants, and then heated at 130 °C with vigorous stirring for 24 hours.
The reaction mixture was then cooled to room temperature, diluted with
acetone and filtered through a small pad of Celite. The filtrate was
concentrated in vacuo and purified by a silica gel packed flash
chromatography column, using acetone/ethyl acetate/hexane (1:1:10) as the
eluent.
N-(2,3,5,6-Tetrafluoro-4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)-3-(trifluoromethyl)-2-naphthamide,
yield 75%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, acetone-d6) δ 10.13 (s, 1H), 8.52 (s, 1H),
8.44 (s, 1H), 8.24-8.18 (m, 2H), 7.83-7.80 (m, 2H); 19F NMR (375 MHz,
acetone-d6) δ -56.06 (t, J = 21.6 Hz, 3F), -58.25 (s, 3F), -142.99 to
-143.10 (m, 2F), -143.47 to -143.56 (m, 2F); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
acetone-d6) δ 165.69, 133.93, 133.02, 130.38, 130.02, 129.92, 129.36,
128.71, 128.40 (q, J = 5.5 Hz), 124.83 (q, J = 32.1 Hz), 124.31 (q, J =
271.3 Hz); HRMS (ESI-TOF) m/z Calcd for C19H8F10NO (M+H)+: 456.0441,
found: 456.0439.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd(II)-Catalyzed Ortho Trifluoromethylation of Arenes and Insights into
the Coordination Mode of Acidic Amide Directing Groups
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Xing-Guo; Dai, Hui-Xiong; Wasa, Masayuki; Yu, Jin-Quan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2012), 134(29), 11948-11951

