$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction conditions: A Schlenk tube charged
with the Togni reagent (II) (0.4 mmol, 126 mg, 2.0 equiv), CuTc (0.02
mmol, 4 mg, 0.1 equiv) and 1 (0.2 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was evacuated and
backfilled with argon (this sequence was repeated three times). MeCN (1.5
mL) was added into the tube. The reaction tube was placed in a pre-heated
80 °C oil bath until compound 1 was consumed completely. The mixture was
allowed to cool to room temperature. The mixture was purified by silica
gel flash chromatography (eluent: petroleum ether). The product 2 in
moderate yield. Compound 2a: 44 mg, 72%, a colorless oil. IR (CH2Cl2): ν
2943, 1580, 1454, 1310, 1264, 1152, 1101, 1028, 908, 734 cm-1; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 2.40 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 2.83 (t, J = 8.0 Hz,
2H), 5.05 (s, 2H), 6.73-6.76 (m, 2H), 7.13 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.28-7.39
(m, 5H), 7.46 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 20.4
(q, J = 1.5 Hz), 27.5, 70.2, 110.5, 120.4, 120.5, 123.3 (q, J = 6.5 Hz),
124.3 (q, J = 269.0 Hz), 126.2 (q, J = 30.6 Hz), 127.2, 128.0, 128.6,
129.9, 136.8, 137.2, 155.2; 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ -68.3; HRMS (EI)
m/z calculated for C18H15OF3 [M+] 304.1075, found 304.1066.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk tube was used, optimized on catalyst, solvent, and temperature,
optimization study, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper(I)-Catalyzed Intramolecular Trifluoromethylation of
Methylenecyclopropanes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
