$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction conditions: A Schlenk tube charged
with the Togni reagent (II) (0.4 mmol, 126 mg, 2.0 equiv), CuTc (0.02
mmol, 4 mg, 0.1 equiv) and 1 (0.2 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was evacuated and
backfilled with argon (this sequence was repeated three times). MeCN (1.5
mL) was added into the tube. The reaction tube was placed in a pre-heated
80 °C oil bath until compound 1 was consumed completely. The mixture was
allowed to cool to room temperature. The mixture was purified by silica
gel flash chromatography (eluent: petroleum ether). The product 2 in
moderate yield. Compound 2m: 36 mg, 70%, a colorless oil. IR (CH2Cl2): ν
2943, 2838, 1660, 1485, 1310, 1259, 1152, 1099, 1042, 796 cm-1; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 2.36-2.41 (m, 2H), 2.87 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H),
3.787 (s, 3H), 3.793 (s, 3H), 6.68 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 6.79 (d, J = 8.8
Hz, 1H), 7.34-7.36 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 19.8, 20.0,
55.8, 55.9, 108.7, 112.1, 121.1, 123.2 (q, J = 6.5 Hz), 124.3 (q, J =
269.1 Hz), 125.0, 126.4 (q, J = 30.6 Hz), 150.3, 150.5; 19F NMR (376 MHz,
CDCl3): δ -68.6; HRMS (EI) m/z calculated for C13H13O2F3 [M+] 258.0868,
found 258.0870.
