$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction conditions: A Schlenk tube charged
with the Togni reagent (II) (0.4 mmol, 126 mg, 2.0 equiv), CuTc (0.02
mmol, 4 mg, 0.1 equiv) and 1 (0.2 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was evacuated and
backfilled with argon (this sequence was repeated three times). MeCN (1.5
mL) was added into the tube. The reaction tube was placed in a pre-heated
80 °C oil bath until compound 1 was consumed completely. The mixture was
allowed to cool to room temperature. The mixture was purified by silica
gel flash chromatography (eluent: petroleum ether). The product 2 in
moderate yield. Compound 2f: 42 mg, 70%, a colorless oil. IR (CH2Cl2): ν
3065, 2842, 1664, 1578, 1311, 1264, 1153, 1095, 905, 694 cm-1; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ 2.41-2.45 (m, 2H), 2.97 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H),
5.08 (s, 2H), 6.81 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 6.90-6.92 (m, 2H), 7.15 (d, J =
8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.31-7.35 (m, 1H), 7.37-7.44 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3, TMS): δ 19.7, 20.2, 70.2, 113.2, 121.0, 123.9, 124.1 (q, J = 269.1
Hz), 127.16, 127.21, 127.7 (q, J = 30.7 Hz), 127.9, 128.6, 128.8 (q, J =
6.5 Hz), 132.4, 137.1, 155.4; 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ -68.9; HRMS
(EI) m/z calculated for C18H15OF3 [M+] 304.1075, found 304.1077.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk tube was used, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
