$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the trifluoromethylation
of arenes and heteroarenes: A dried Young-type NMR tube was charged with
1-(Trifluoromethyl)-1,2-benziodoxol-3(1H)-one (1, 12.6 mg, 0,04 mmol),
100 μL of a stock solution of perfluoronaphthalene in CDCl3 containing
0.01 mmol (used as internal standard) and 100 μL of a freshly prepared
stock solution of methyltrioxorhenium (MTO) in CDCl3 containing 0.08
equivalents (0.003 mmol). To the colourless solution 1.5 equivalents
(0,06 mmol) of the aromatic substrate were added and CDCl3 was added to
afford a final volume of 0.5 mL. The tube was closed and the mixture was
heated at 70 °C for a certain amount of time (until the colour changed to
dark brown-black). The mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature
and after the corresponding NMR analysis, filtrated through a plug of
alumina-N eluting with acetone. The resulting colourless filtrate was
then subject to characterization by GC-MS.
1,4-dimethoxy-2-(trifluoromethyl)benzene[8](Table 2, Entry 6) Yield = 70%
(5% of ditrifluoromethylated products). 19F NMR (188 MHz, CDCl3) δ -55.11
(s, di-CF3), -62.37 (s, mono-CF3), - 62.83 (s, di-CF3). GC-MS: Ret. time
= 38.77 min (monotrifluoromethylated product), EI-MS m/z = 206.0 [M]+,
191.0 [M-CH3]+, 187.0 [M-F]+. 40.15 min (ditrifluoromethylated product),
EI-MS m/z = 274.0 [M]+, 259.0 [M-CH3]+, 255.0 [M-F]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
